# Machine settings for the fine-tuning and simulation scripts
# (scripts/local_config.sh). Copy to config/local.env, which git ignores,
# and set what differs on this machine. Leave a line out to take its
# default; with no file everything runs on this machine. A variable set
# in the environment wins over this file.

# The host holding the rounds and the shared mailbox, as ssh names it.
# Empty: this machine.
REMOTE=
# Paths on REMOTE (relative to its home) of the rounds folder and the
# shared mailbox. Default with REMOTE: bdbv-rounds and bdbv-mailbox.md.
#REMOTE_ROOT=bdbv-rounds
#REMOTE_MAILBOX=bdbv-mailbox.md

# On the machine that simulates (scripts/sim_rounds*.sh): its rounds
# folder and mailbox. Default: $HOME/bdbv-rounds and $HOME/bdbv-mailbox.md.
#ROOT=$HOME/bdbv-rounds
#MAILBOX=$HOME/bdbv-mailbox.md

# This machine's name in mailbox lines and manifests. Default: hostname -s.
#HOST_NAME=sims-host
# An optional local copy of this machine's mailbox lines.
#INBOX=output/inbox.md

# Simulation slots and memory caps (scripts/sim_rounds.sh).
#SLOTS=3
#SLOT_MEM=16G
#RETRY_MEM=20G
#MIN_FREE_GB=20
#MIN_DISK_GB=16
# The same for a second machine (scripts/sim_rounds_laptop.sh).
#SLOT_MEM_GB=16
#RETRY_MEM_GB=20

# The r3 driver's remote worktree (scripts/finetune_driver.sh).
#REMOTE_DIR=path/to/repo/worktree

# The trainer's device: auto (CUDA, then MPS, then CPU), cuda, mps or cpu.
#DEVICE=auto
# PyTorch's MPS memory watermark, on Apple GPUs.
#MPS_HIGH_WATERMARK=0.85
# Hugging Face cache of the base model.
#HF_HOME=output/finetune/hf

# The top-level workflow (workflow/Snakefile, `task simulate`, ...).
# The fine-tuning run's folder: its simulations, segments and checkpoints
# n<N>/. Default: $ROOT/checkpoints/slots.
#RUN=$ROOT/checkpoints/slots
# The checkpoint scores' cache. Default: $ROOT/scores.
#SCORE_CACHE=$ROOT/scores
# The slots check's no-slots run (n<K>/ folders) and German blocks.
# Defaults: $ROOT/checkpoints and $ROOT/germany/germany.pkl.
#NOSLOTS_RUN=$ROOT/checkpoints
#GERMANY_BLOCKS=$ROOT/germany/germany.pkl
# A command prefix capping one job's memory; {mem} becomes its budget,
# such as 16384M. Empty: no cap (the laptop).
#JOB_PREFIX='systemd-run --user --scope -q -p MemoryMax={mem} -p MemorySwapMax=0'
# Cores and memory budget (MB) the workflow may use on this machine.
#CORES=4
#MEM_MB=32768
# What `task all` runs on this machine, from simulate, finetune and score
# (archie: simulate score; the laptop: finetune). Default: all three.
#TARGETS="simulate finetune score"
# Where the trainer's batches come from: local (this machine's rounds) or
# release (the sims-r<N> releases). Default: workflow/config.yaml's.
#SIMS_FROM=release
# Release each checkpoint as soon as it is trained (the laptop).
#PUBLISH=1
# Mailbox lines from the workflow (round ready, checkpoint saved or
# published, scores landed, failures); any value turns them on.
#NOTIFY=1
# Simulation batches at once (at most 2 on archie).
#SIM_SLOTS=2
# The fine-tuning dashboard's runs with a local folder (task dashboard),
# specs separated by `;`: name=<folder|prefix>[,label=..][,colour=..]
# [,live][,base=..][,prefix=..][,hashes=h1+h2][,n=h1:250+h2:500].
#DASHBOARD_RUNS="slots=output/finetune/continuous-slots,prefix=slots-,live"
# Where the scores are on REMOTE, when not REMOTE_ROOT/scores.
#REMOTE_SCORE_CACHE=bdbv-rounds/scores
